From: Ethan Lee <ethantlee21@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] feat: make the session daemon its own responsible process on macOS

macOS attributes privacy-gated operations (Local Network, TCC) to a
process's *responsible process*, fixed at spawn and inherited from the
parent, so a session created by `zmx attach` was attributed to the app
that ran it, and to nothing once that app quit: every survivor becomes
responsible for itself and a client reattaching over the socket never
re-attributes it. Each program in the session was then judged by its own
identity, which for anything not Apple-signed meant local network access
refused with EHOSTUNREACH and no prompt (macterm#419).

Responsibility cannot be changed after the fact, but the disclaim exists
as a spawn attribute and POSIX_SPAWN_SETEXEC lets the forked child apply
it to itself by exec'ing in place: same pid, session and fds. The daemon
re-execs as `zmx __daemon <session> [-- command...]` with the rest of its
state in ZMX_DAEMON_* variables consumed before the shell exists, and
falls back to the forked image if that fails. Its code signature's
identifier is what macOS then asks the user about; Macterm signs its
bundled copy as the app itself. Linux is unchanged; the bats file pins the
contract on Darwin and skips elsewhere.
---
diff --git a/src/daemonize.zig b/src/daemonize.zig
index 800431b..98be69a 100644
--- a/src/daemonize.zig
+++ b/src/daemonize.zig
@@ -1,4 +1,5 @@
 const std = @import("std");
+const builtin = @import("builtin");
 const lib_posix = @import("posix.zig");
 const Cfg = @import("cfg.zig");
 const socket = @import("socket.zig");
@@ -124,6 +125,161 @@ pub fn spawnPty(sesh_name: []const u8, cmd: Cmd, size: ipc.Resize) !PtyInfo {
